  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients with the update, performance, drift, feature and subgroup tools (spending 3 epsilon on each of the four main screens, 2 on each of two subgroup screens), then used the last 4 epsilon to re-check two leads. Three clients stand out clearly: AZ, IA and MN upload updates about 13\u201317x the median norm pointing almost exactly against the consensus (cosine about -0.97 to -0.99) in every round from round 1. That is a sign-flipped, scaled poisoning pattern, and their local performance rows look normal. I did not report: VI (its feature anomalies in the screen did not reproduce on the narrower re-query); PR (update cosine consistently lower, about 0.67 on average, but still positive, with normal local AUC/calibration and no other corroborating statistic; a possible label-noise or heterogeneity case, low confidence); GU, DC, WV and the subgroup outliers (WI age group 5, OK age group 7), which are single weak z-values from small clients. The budget is fully spent."
